Because $AC=12$ and $AM=x$, $MC=12-x$. Let $MN=z$. Then, because $MNPC$ is a rectangle, $NP=12-x$ and $PC=z$, and so $BP=5-z$. By AA similarity, $\triangle AMN \sim \triangle NPB$. From this similarity, we can solve the following proportion for $z$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{BP}{PN} &= \frac{NM}{AM} \\
\frac{5-z}{12-x} &= \frac z x \\
5x-xz &= 12z-xz \\
5x &= 12z \\
z &= \frac{5x}{12}
\end{aligned}
$$

Because $y=MN+NP=z+12-x$, we can now substitute for $z$ and find $y$ in terms of $x$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y &= z+12-x \\
&= \frac{5x}{12}-x+12 \\
&= \frac{-7x}{12}+\frac{144}{12} \\
&= \frac{144-7x}{12}
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus, our answer is $\boxed{\textbf{(C) }\frac{144-7x}{12}}$.

